---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// AI-drafted starter template. Have a lawyer review before relying on this
// document for a paid product launch. Placeholders to fill before publishing
// are marked [LIKE THIS].
const effectiveDate = '2026-04-18';
const lastReviewed = '2026-04-18';
---

<Layout
  title="Limnia · Privacy"
  description="What Limnia collects, what it doesn't, and where your data goes."
>
  <main class="relative z-10">
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pt-20 pb-24 sm:px-10 sm:pt-28">
      <header class="mb-14 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-12">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-faint md:col-span-3">
          / privacy
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-9">
          <h1 class="font-display text-[40px] font-semibold leading-[1.03] tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-[56px]">
            Privacy.
          </h1>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[17px] leading-[1.6] text-ink-muted">
            Limnia collects nothing about how you use it. The whole policy is
            short because there isn't much to say.
          </p>
          <dl class="mt-6 inline-grid grid-cols-[8rem_1fr] gap-x-3 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em]">
            <dt class="text-ink-faint">effective</dt><dd class="text-ink">{effectiveDate}</dd>
            <dt class="text-ink-faint">last reviewed</dt><dd class="text-ink">{lastReviewed}</dd>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </header>

      <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-12 text-[16.5px] leading-[1.65] text-ink-muted">

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-[24px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">
            1. The application
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Limnia runs entirely on your device. It makes no network requests
            during normal use. There is no telemetry, no analytics SDK, no crash
            reporting service, no auto-update phone-home. The binary is roughly
            2&nbsp;MB. Most of that is the drawing engine, not data plumbing.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Specifically, Limnia does <em class="text-ink not-italic">not</em>
            collect:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2 pl-0">
            {[
              'How often you use it',
              'Which tools or colors you pick',
              'What you draw, save, or copy',
              'Your operating system version, hardware, or display configuration',
              'Any identifier that could be tied back to you',
            ].map((item) => (
              <li class="grid grid-cols-[1.25rem_1fr] items-baseline gap-2">
                <span class="font-mono text-[12px] text-ink-faint">▸</span>
                <span>{item}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-[24px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">
            2. What Limnia writes locally
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Limnia stores a small amount of data on your device, never
            transmitted off it:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-3 pl-0">
            <li class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-1">
              <span class="font-mono text-[12.5px] text-pen">%APPDATA%\Limnia\config.json</span>
              <span>Your last-used tool, color, and brush size. Written so Limnia restores state when you reopen it.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-1">
              <span class="font-mono text-[12.5px] text-pen">%APPDATA%\Limnia\crash.log</span>
              <span>Diagnostic information if Limnia crashes. Stays on your device unless you choose to share it when reporting a bug.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-1">
              <span class="font-mono text-[12.5px] text-pen">PNG exports</span>
              <span>Screenshots you save go wherever you choose. Limnia doesn't keep its own copy.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You can delete the AppData folder at any time. Uninstalling Limnia
            via Windows leaves it intact on purpose, so a reinstall keeps your
            settings.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-[24px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">
            3. This website
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The Limnia landing page is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may log
            incoming requests as part of standard server operation; see
            <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-pen">GitHub's privacy statement</a>
            for what they retain. We don't run analytics, trackers, or cookie
            banners on this site.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If you submit your email through the Mac-interest or Pro-waitlist
            forms, your address is sent to <a href="https://tally.so/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-pen">Tally</a>,
            a third-party form processor (see Tally's
            <a href="https://tally.so/help/gdpr" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-pen">privacy notice</a>).
            We use that email only to notify you when the relevant thing ships.
            Email us to be removed at any time.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-[24px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">
            4. Payments (Pro, when it ships)
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            When Limnia Pro launches, payments are processed by third parties
            who handle billing, tax, and refunds:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-3 pl-0">
            <li class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-1">
              <span class="font-mono text-[12.5px] text-highlight">Lemon Squeezy</span>
              <span>Direct purchases through this site. Lemon Squeezy is the merchant of record and sees your name, email, billing address, and payment method. See <a href="https://www.lemonsqueezy.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-pen">their privacy policy</a>.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-1">
              <span class="font-mono text-[12.5px] text-highlight">Microsoft Store</span>
              <span>Purchases through the Microsoft Store are handled by Microsoft. See Microsoft's privacy statement.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We receive your order details and email solely to deliver your
            license key.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-[24px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">
            5. Children
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Limnia is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly
            collect data from children.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-[24px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">
            6. Changes to this policy
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If we materially change anything here, the effective date at the top
            updates and a note is added to the
            <a href="/limnia-site/changelog" class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-pen">changelog</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-[24px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">
            7. Contact
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Questions about this policy or about your data:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2 pl-0">
            <li class="grid grid-cols-[6rem_1fr] items-baseline gap-3 font-mono text-[13px]">
              <span class="uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-faint">email</span>
              <a href="mailto:[YOUR_SUPPORT_EMAIL]" class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-pen">[YOUR_SUPPORT_EMAIL]</a>
            </li>
            <li class="grid grid-cols-[6rem_1fr] items-baseline gap-3 font-mono text-[13px]">
              <span class="uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-faint">issues</span>
              <a href="https://github.com/vijo0018/limnia-site/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ink underline decoration-line-strong underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-pen">github.com/vijo0018/limnia-site/issues</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <p class="border-t border-line pt-8 font-mono text-[11.5px] text-ink-faint">
          Limnia is operated by [YOUR FULL NAME / BUSINESS NAME], based in
          [YOUR COUNTRY / STATE].
        </p>

      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
